ready: 1
kind: rule
id: retention.rule.strength
display_id: RULE-RETENTION-STRENGTH
module: retention
title: How strong a memory is
summary: A memory's strength falls with the time since it was last used, more slowly for salient memories,
  and decides whether it is active, dormant or forgotten.
inputs:
- name: memory
  source: The memory record
  source_kind: stored
- name: now
  source: The sweep's clock
  source_kind: derived
- name: decay settings
  source: The stack's decay configuration
  source_kind: config
decision:
  nodes:
  - id: in
    node_kind: input
    text: One memory at sweep time
    refs:
    - memory.data.memory
  - id: keep
    node_kind: decision
    text: Is it protected, a value, a foundational belief, or tied to the active self-narrative?
  - id: full
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Strength stays at full; status unchanged
  - id: sup
    node_kind: decision
    text: Is it superseded?
  - id: supout
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Unchanged; superseded memories are kept for history until their source is purged
  - id: calc
    node_kind: calc
    text: Strength is one minus idle days over the kind's window stretched by salience
    refs:
    - retention.const.idle-windows
  - id: zero
    node_kind: decision
    text: Has strength reached zero?
  - id: forgot
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Forgotten, recoverable until the recovery window ends
    refs:
    - retention.const.forget-recovery-days
  - id: dorm
    node_kind: decision
    text: Is strength below the dormancy threshold?
    refs:
    - retention.const.dormant-below
  - id: dormant
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Dormant, when currently active
  - id: active
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Active, when currently dormant because it was used again
  edges:
  - from: in
    to: keep
  - from: keep
    to: full
    label: 'yes'
  - from: keep
    to: sup
    label: 'no'
  - from: sup
    to: supout
    label: 'yes'
  - from: sup
    to: calc
    label: 'no'
  - from: calc
    to: zero
  - from: zero
    to: forgot
    label: 'yes'
  - from: zero
    to: dorm
    label: 'no'
  - from: dorm
    to: dormant
    label: 'yes'
  - from: dorm
    to: active
    label: 'no'
calculations:
- name: idle_days
  expr: (now − last_used_at) in days, where last_used_at starts at created_at
- name: window
  expr: idle window for the kind × (1 + salience)
- name: strength
  expr: clamp(1 − idle_days ÷ window, 0, 1)
sets:
- name: use
  members:
  - the agent opens a memory by id or from a search result
  - helped feedback
  - a gut check fires on a guardrail
  - sleep reinforces the memory
  - an explicit update or revision
  - recovery from forgotten
- name: not use
  members:
  - inclusion in a load, the session index or a cue
  - appearing in search results
  - an owner browsing from the command line
constants:
- retention.const.idle-windows
- retention.const.dormant-below
- retention.const.forget-recovery-days
rationale: Idle time counts from the last use, not from creation, so a memory that keeps helping lives
  indefinitely and one that never helps fades even if it was once important. Salience stretches the window
  because an intense experience earns a longer memory, which is how appraisal shapes forgetting. Inclusion
  is not use, otherwise every loaded memory would refresh itself each session and never fade. The identity
  core does not fade, because the agent's values and sense of itself should change by revision, not by
  neglect. Strength is computed from stored times, so a read never changes it and sync never sees it as
  an edit.
